            <div xml:id="d809">

                <pb facs="0766" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12756: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-03T09:00:00+02:00">July 3, 1941—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:28 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>265. My 259, July 1, noon. Head of the Lebanese Government have sent me signed
                    note giving full details re damage caused in Beirut by raids during nights June
                    29th to 30th and June 30th to July 1st. He concludes with the statement that
                    only objectives devoid of all military character were hit which has caused
                    considerable emotion among the civilian inhabitants. Lebanese Government
                    protests energetically and requests me to intervene so as to put an end to
                    useless destruction of property and innocent lives.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
